text=[@these instructions describe how to create a basic ltsp system where all the%0aapplications are running locally with an anonymous login, using gdm, for i386%0ahardware.  non-anonymous login with ldap or some other authentiation mechanism%0awith writeable home directories is definitely possible, but not described here.%0aand of course, you could probably use kdm insead of gdm, with a few changes.%0a%0ainstall the ltsp-server package:%0a%0aapt-get install ltsp-server%0a%0a%0abuild the client environment:%0a%0altsp-build-client%0a%0a%0ainstall a desktop environment:%0a%0achroot /opt/ltsp/i386 tasksel install desktop%0a(alternately: chroot /opt/ltsp/i386 apt-get install gdm %3cand other packages>)%0a%0a%0aadd an anonymous user for autologin:%0a%0achroot /opt/ltsp/i386 adduser --disabled-password --gecos ,,, autologin%0a%0a(note: you may want to ensure a specific --uid and --gid, too)%0a%0a%0amake /home and /var/lib/gdm writeable:%0a%0aecho 'copy_dirs="$copy_dirs /home"' >> /opt/ltsp/i386/etc/default/ltsp-client-setup%0aecho 'rw_dirs="$rw_dirs /var/lib/gdm"' >> /opt/ltsp/i386/etc/default/ltsp-client-setup%0a%0a%0ato /opt/ltsp/i386/etc/gdm/gdm.conf, add the following lines in the daemon%0asection, like so:%0a%0a[daemon]%0aAutomaticLoginEnable=true%0aAutomaticLogin=autologin%0aTimedLoginEnable=true%0aTimedLogin=autologin%0aTimedLoginDelay=30%0a@]
time=1239067613
