diff:1239067613:1239067613:=1,45d0%0a%3c [@these instructions describe how to create a basic ltsp system where all the%0a%3c applications are running locally with an anonymous login, using gdm, for i386%0a%3c hardware.  non-anonymous login with ldap or some other authentiation mechanism%0a%3c with writeable home directories is definitely possible, but not described here.%0a%3c and of course, you could probably use kdm insead of gdm, with a few changes.%0a%3c %0a%3c install the ltsp-server package:%0a%3c %0a%3c apt-get install ltsp-server%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c build the client environment:%0a%3c %0a%3c ltsp-build-client%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c install a desktop environment:%0a%3c %0a%3c chroot /opt/ltsp/i386 tasksel install desktop%0a%3c (alternately: chroot /opt/ltsp/i386 apt-get install gdm %3cand other packages>)%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c add an anonymous user for autologin:%0a%3c %0a%3c chroot /opt/ltsp/i386 adduser --disabled-password --gecos ,,, autologin%0a%3c %0a%3c (note: you may want to ensure a specific --uid and --gid, too)%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c make /home and /var/lib/gdm writeable:%0a%3c %0a%3c echo 'copy_dirs="$copy_dirs /home"' >> /opt/ltsp/i386/etc/default/ltsp-client-setup%0a%3c echo 'rw_dirs="$rw_dirs /var/lib/gdm"' >> /opt/ltsp/i386/etc/default/ltsp-client-setup%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c to /opt/ltsp/i386/etc/gdm/gdm.conf, add the following lines in the daemon%0a%3c section, like so:%0a%3c %0a%3c [daemon]%0a%3c AutomaticLoginEnable=true%0a%3c AutomaticLogin=autologin%0a%3c TimedLoginEnable=true%0a%3c TimedLogin=autologin%0a%3c TimedLoginDelay=30%0a%3c @]%0a\ No newline at end of file%0a
host:1239067613=189.35.184.218
